    "97a3c888-87e7-4e19-8b87-8bb3485410c8": {
      "type": "text-and-image",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Damascus_Advent_Study_Book_6.jpg",
        "image_mask": "none",
        "image2_mask": "none",
        "subtitle": "DAMASCUS",
        "title": "From The Introduction",
        "text": "<p>If we let it, Advent can be so much more than an ancient practice or an annual tradition. It can be a sacred season during which we discover how Christmas is more than a story of a birth—it’s a story of rebirth, too. A story of miraculous transformation and undeserved redemption, much like the one Paul experienced on the road to Damascus. Paul, too, was well acquainted with the rules and religious practices but lacked a real relationship with Jesus until that miraculous encounter. I want us to have a similar encounter this Advent; one that takes this season from stressful to sacred and from performative to transformative.</p><p>- <em>Hannah Jessen Conway</em>, author</p>",
