    "300b442e-c30a-43b8-aef7-784a2c15a66b": {
      "type": "text-and-image",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Author_Shoot_Hannah_1.jpg",
        "image_mask": "none",
        "image2_mask": "none",
        "subtitle": "MEET THE AUTHOR",
        "title": "Hannah Jessen Conway",
        "text": "<p>Hannah Jessen Conway loves words—reading them, writing them, and, most recently, learning to sign them. She lives in Raleigh, North Carolina, with her husband and two wild and wonderful boys. She’s a beach girl at heart, a Tar Heel fanatic, and the author of <em>Love Sounds Like</em>, a children’s book inspired by her deaf son. With a background in nonprofit marketing, Hannah now seeks to use her writing to point others back to the Author of our faith. You can connect with her by visiting HJConway.com or on Instagram.</p>",
        "button_label": "FOLLOW HANNAH HERE",
        "button_link": "https://www.instagram.com/hannah_jessen_conway/",
        "button_style": "primary",
        "align_text": "left",
        "image_width": "50",
        "layout": "right",
        "divider": false,
        "top_padding": true,
        "bottom_padding": true,
        "lazyload_images": true
      }
    },
    "fa90acba-9c86-4dbf-915e-68c375d60143": {
      "type": "text-and-image",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Author_Shoot_Hannah.jpg",
        "image_mask": "none",
        "image2_mask": "none",
        "subtitle": "MEET THE AUTHOR",
        "title": "Hannah’s Story",
        "text": "<p>I grew up in a Christian family, and so the practices of Advent were familiar. And while these traditions marked the holiday season for me, I failed to grasp what Advent meant for my own walk with the Lord until I was older. In my early 20s, I began to understand for the first time how the Christmas story wasn’t just something of the past—it provided hope for my present and, even more significantly, for my future. </p><p>Since then, Advent has been my favorite season. As November draws to a close each year, I can feel myself becoming more expectant, more excited about what God is going to teach me. Rather than letting life's hardship drive us further from Advent, I pray it beckons us toward it. We don’t have to be “ready” for Advent. We can come as we are, knowing that Jesus will meet us in the middle of our messy stories, just like he entered into our messy world more than 2,000 years ago. </p>",
        "button_label": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "button_style": "primary",
        "align_text": "left",
        "image_width": "50",
        "layout": "left",
        "divider": false,
        "top_padding": true,
        "bottom_padding": true,
        "lazyload_images": true
      }
    },
    "text_and_image_3MkzaG": {
      "type": "text-and-image",
      "name": "t:sections.text-and-image.presets.image_with_text.name",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Hannah_Author_Shoot_5.jpg",
        "image_mask": "none",
        "image2_mask": "none",
        "subtitle": "",
        "title": "",
        "text": "<p>That was the impetus for writing <em>Damascus</em>: to remind us all that Advent can be so much more than an ancient practice or an annual tradition, if we let it. It can be a sacred season during which we discover how Christmas is more than a story of a birth—it’s a story of rebirth, too. A story of miraculous transformation and undeserved redemption, much like the one Paul experienced on the road to Damascus. Paul, too, was well acquainted with the rules and religious practices but lacked a real relationship with Jesus until that miraculous encounter. I want us to have a similar encounter this Advent; one that takes this season from stressful to sacred and from performative to transformative.</p><p>I hope that you’ll join me this Advent as we discover how Christmas still has the power to change everything. Let’s not merely survive the holiday season—let’s embrace the wonder of Christmas and celebrate the hope that it gives us, not just for this life, but for the next. </p>",
        "button_label": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "button_style": "primary",
        "align_text": "left",
        "image_width": "50",
        "layout": "right",
        "divider": false,
        "top_padding": true,
        "bottom_padding": true,
        "lazyload_images": true
      }
    },
